    "ai_summary": {
      "id": 844114,
      "summarized_text": "A Shopify product CSV import completed with 1,054 products imported and 14 rejected. The reported error lines extend beyond the 1,845 lines visible in the spreadsheet, making the affected rows difficult to locate. One reply suggested checking the variant column; a later, more detailed response explained that Shopify’s parsed line numbers may differ because of headers, blank lines, or line breaks in descriptions, and recommended locating the affected products by Handle (the product identifier) and SKU instead of relying on row numbers.\n\nThe errors point to three variant-option issues: duplicate option combinations under the same Handle, missing values for a named Size option, and duplicate “Default Title” variants. Suggested fixes are to check each affected product’s options, fill in or remove blank Size fields, and ensure Default Title is used only once for products without real options. The response also advises saving as UTF-8 CSV with description line breaks and quotes properly formatted, then reimporting the corrected products. The thread offers guidance but does not confirm that the import was fixed.",
